//? Title: Siamese verification and unseen-class one-shot tasks
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Shared convolutional features turn two images into a symmetric learned similarity score. Hand derivatives and full-width checks precede visible tensor Adam fitting on MNIST digits0–4,checkpoint selection on5–6,and actual one-shot previews on unseen7–9.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/siamese.cpp`.

> The method

Learn a weighted absolute difference between two shared sigmoid embeddings with binary cross entropy. Use the highest query/support score to classify one-shot tasks without fine-tuning;keep class-disjoint selection,optimizer loops and baseline comparisons visible.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/siamese_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/siamese_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/siamese_concept.tikz > build/siamese_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/siamese_concept.svg build/siamese_concept.dvi > build/siamese_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
