> Full and compact encoders really share parameters

The full105-pixel model uses VALID10/7/4/4 convolutions with64/128/128/256
channels,max pooling after the first three,and a4096-dimensional sigmoid
embedding. Including the similarity head,it has38,951,745 learned scalars in
12 tensors. The compact48-pixel encoder keeps all four convolutions and three
pools,using kernels5/3/3/2,channels8/16/16/32 and64 embedding coordinates:
24,337 learned scalars in the same12 tensor roles. Pre-pool sides are44/20/8/3.
The full graph below executes a forward/backward pass;it is not just a census.
The compact native fixture also verifies that encoder gradients equal the sum
of the two separately stopped-branch contributions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    const auto c = compact ? n::models::SiameseConfig::Compact() : n::models::SiameseConfig{};
    n::ParameterStore p(17);
    const auto x = n::arange(0, c.side * c.side * 2).reshape({2, c.side, c.side, 1});
    const auto a = n::models::SiameseEncoder(p, .5 + .45 * n::sin(x * .173), c),
               b = n::models::SiameseEncoder(p, .5 + .45 * n::cos(x * .097), c);
    const auto z = n::models::SiameseLogit(p, a.embedding, b.embedding, c.embedding);
    const auto gradients = n::grad(n::sum(z), p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != (compact ? 24337 : 38951745) || gradients.size() != 12)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &g : gradients)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(g.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print(
        "{}:{} learned scalars,12 shared leaves and finite gradients;embedding[2,{}].\n",
        compact ? "Compact48" : "Full105", p.count(), c.embedding);
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full105:38951745 learned scalars,12 shared leaves and finite gradients;embedding[2,4096].
Compact48:24337 learned scalars,12 shared leaves and finite gradients;embedding[2,64].
// result_end

> Actual pairs and disjoint classes

We use the official60,000/10,000 MNIST train/test IDX splits from the existing
local cache. Fitting uses only digits0–4 from the training split;validation
uses digits5–6 from that split;testing uses only digits7–9 from the official
test split. Each selected class contributes its first512 rows. Host RNG
selects row/class metadata;pixel gathering and all image arithmetic use tensors.

Balanced pair sampling creates exactly half same-class and half different-class
pairs,then shuffles them. Same-class rows are distinct. One-shot tasks have one
support per class and a different query image of one support class. No query
fine-tuning or test-time optimizer updates occur. The displayed images are the
actual sampled rows,not generated digit illustrations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/siamese_pairs.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto data = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  const auto buckets = n::models::SiameseBuckets(data, {0, 1, 2, 3, 4});
  const auto pairs = n::models::SiamesePairs(buckets, 16, 11);
  std::vector<std::size_t> rows;
  int positives = 0;
  std::print("| row | left digit | right digit | same target |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  const auto labels = n::models::MetricDatasetLabels(data);
  for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
    rows.push_back(pairs[i].left);
    rows.push_back(pairs[i].right);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, labels[pairs[i].left], labels[pairs[i].right],
               int(pairs[i].same));
  }
  for (const auto &p : pairs)
    positives += int(p.same);
  if (positives != 8)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::models::SiameseImages(data, rows), "build/siamese_pairs.png", 2, 0, 1,
                     2, 1, 4);
  std::print("\n16 sampled pairs: exactly 8 same and 8 different; first 8 shown as left and "
             "right. Source "
             "rows and labels stay aligned.\n");
}
```
